{
  "title": "The first condition of Salah – cleanliness",
  "pages": "37",
  "intro": "A clean body, clean clothes and a clean place to pray.",
  "learn": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "html": "Allah loves tidiness and cleanliness – especially when we pray. So the <b>first condition</b> of Salah is: a clean <b>body</b>, clean <b>clothes</b> and a clean <b>place</b> to pray."
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "title": "Hadith",
      "html": "Muhammad (SAW) said: <i>“Cleanliness is half of iman.”</i> <small>(Muslim)</small>"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "🧼 A clean body"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "personal hygiene",
        "washing the hands often",
        "brushing the teeth",
        "making wudu",
        "bathing regularly",
        "keeping clean in the toilet",
        "cutting the nails"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "👕 Clean clothes"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "html": "We keep our clothes clean and tidy, away from all impurity – especially alcohol, blood, urine and a dog’s saliva. We wash, clean and iron them regularly."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "🕌 A clean place"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "html": "Allah made the <b>whole earth</b> a place where we can pray. The place must be clean and tidy, so we use a <b>prayer mat</b> (sajjadah). Where we pray there must be no pictures or figures of living beings, or anything that distracts us."
    }
  ],
